msgctxt "#32137"
msgid "New Content Detection"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32138"
msgid "Periodically check for new content"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32139"
msgid "Chronicle can tell this device when new TV content has been imported that Kodi hasn't discovered yet (VideoLibrary.Refresh, used everywhere else, only works on an item Kodi already has -- discovering a brand-new episode file needs a real library scan). This device always checks once when Kodi starts, regardless of this setting. Turning this on also checks periodically while Kodi keeps running, at the interval below -- off by default, since most imports happen on Chronicle's own nightly schedule and are already caught by the next Kodi startup. Only ever scans the source folder(s) this addon is actually the configured scraper for on this device, never anything else."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32140"
msgid "Check every (minutes)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32141"
msgid "How often the periodic check runs, in 30-minute steps. Defaults to every 2 hours (120 minutes)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32150"
msgid "Library Repair"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32151"
msgid "Repair Stuck Episodes -- Preview"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32152"
msgid "Occasionally, removing a TV show from Kodi's library doesn't fully clean up after itself: specific episode files can end up permanently stuck, where Kodi will never ask this scraper about them again no matter how many times you remove the show and rescan. This isn't a Chronicle problem or a scraper failure -- it's Kodi's own library database still believing that exact file was already scanned in, for a show that no longer exists. If a show has ever stayed stuck missing certain episodes through repeated full rescans, this is almost always why. This checks this device's own Kodi library for that specific kind of stuck (\"orphaned\") entry and shows you exactly what it found -- nothing is changed. Use \"Repair Stuck Episodes\" below to actually fix what this finds."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32153"
msgid "Repair Stuck Episodes"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32154"
msgid "Checks this device's own Kodi library for episodes permanently stuck the way \"Preview\" above describes, shows you exactly what it found before touching anything, and -- only if you confirm -- removes just those broken entries so Kodi will properly re-examine the real files on your next scan. A safety backup of your Kodi library database is always made first, and nothing else in your library is touched."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32155"
msgid "Undo Last Repair"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#32156"
msgid "Reverses exactly the most recent \"Repair Stuck Episodes\" run on this device, and nothing else -- restores only the specific entries that run removed, from the safety backup it made at the time. Does not undo anything older than the single most recent repair. Safe to use even if you've since rescanned or watched something: anything added to your library since the repair is left completely alone."
msgstr ""

